  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'In July 2025, the Ministry of Health of Bhutan confirmed a cluster of acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS) cases among the 69th batch of Desuup trainees in Dewathang. Laboratory tests and epidemiological investigations identified leptospirosis as the cause. Tragically, 3 Desuups died from the infection.
(a) Describe the causative agent of leptospirosis and explain how it is commonly transmitted to humans.
(b) As a healthcare professional, list five preventive measures you would implement to control the spread of leptospirosis in the community. (3 marks)', '(a) Leptospirosis is caused by Leptospira interrogans, a thin, coiled, motile spirochete bacterium. Infected animals, especially rats, cattle, pigs and dogs, pass it in their urine; humans are infected when water, mud or soil contaminated with this urine comes into contact with cuts, abrasions or mucous membranes (eyes, mouth), for example while training, farming or wading through floodwater. (b) Preventive measures: control rodents around camps and homes; avoid swimming or wading in stagnant or flood water; wear boots, gloves and protective clothing; provide safe drinking water and proper sanitation; vaccinate livestock and dogs; educate people on early symptoms and seek early treatment; give doxycycline prophylaxis to high-risk groups such as trainees during exposure.', null, '[{"point": "Agent: Leptospira (interrogans), a spiral, motile spirochete bacterium", "marks": 0.5}, {"point": "Transmission: contact of skin cuts/mucous membranes with water, soil or mud contaminated by urine of infected rats, cattle, dogs; not person to person", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Five preventive measures (e.g. rodent control, avoid wading in floodwater, protective boots and gloves, safe water, vaccinate animals, awareness, early treatment / doxycycline prophylaxis for high-risk groups)", "marks": 1.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
