  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Mr. Dophu, a 47-year-old man, has been experiencing difficulty seeing nearby objects clearly, while distant objects appear normal. After a vision test, he is diagnosed with presbyopia, a common age-related condition.
(a) What type of lens would be recommended to correct Mr. Dophu''s vision problem?
(b) Explain the principle behind how this lens helps improve near vision. Support your explanation with a ray diagram (describe it). (3 marks)', '(a) A convex (converging) lens, as reading glasses or the lower part of bifocals. (b) In presbyopia the eye lens becomes less elastic and the ciliary muscles weaken, so the eye cannot increase its power to focus near objects; the near point moves farther away and light from a nearby object would focus behind the retina. A convex lens adds converging power: it bends the rays inward before they enter the eye, producing a virtual image of the object at the man''s own near point, so the eye can focus it sharply on the retina. Ray diagram: an object at 25 cm, rays passing through the convex lens and converging so that they meet on the retina instead of behind it.', null, '[{"point": "A convex (converging) lens / reading glasses (or bifocals)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "With age the eye lens loses flexibility; near point recedes; light from near objects focuses behind the retina", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Convex lens converges rays before they enter the eye, forming a virtual image at the eye''s near point so the image falls on the retina (diagram: rays from a near object bent inward by the lens, meeting on the retina)", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'medical-science-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
