  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Name the parts labelled 1-7 of the female reproductive system (see the diagram) and state one function of each part. (No need to draw the diagram.) (3 marks)', '1 Vagina: receives sperm and is the birth canal. 2 Cervix: neck of the uterus; produces mucus and dilates during childbirth. 3 Uterine cavity / endometrium: where the embryo implants and is nourished. 4 Ovary: produces ova and the hormones oestrogen and progesterone. 5 Fimbriae: finger-like projections that sweep the released ovum into the oviduct. 6 Fallopian tube (oviduct): carries the ovum to the uterus; usual site of fertilisation. 7 Fundus (body) of the uterus with myometrium: its muscle contracts to expel the baby during labour.', null, '[{"point": "1 Vagina - birth canal, receives sperm; 2 Cervix - opening of uterus, mucus, dilates in birth", "marks": 1}, {"point": "3 Uterus cavity / endometrium - implantation and nourishment of embryo; 4 Ovary - produces ova and oestrogen/progesterone", "marks": 1}, {"point": "5 Fimbriae - sweep ovum into oviduct; 6 Fallopian tube (oviduct) - site of fertilisation, carries ovum; 7 Fundus / body of uterus (myometrium) - contractions in labour", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
