  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'You are working in the surgical ward and have just assisted in a minor surgical procedure (wound debridement). Following the procedure, several types of waste have been generated and you are responsible for segregating them:
- Blood-stained gauze and cotton
- Used gloves and surgical mask
- Used syringe with needle
- Empty plastic IV fluid bottle
- Broken glass ampoule of medication
- Used scalpel blade
- Leftover food and a tissue paper from the patient''s bedside
Identify the type of biomedical waste that each represents and state the appropriate colour-coded bin for each, according to biomedical waste management guidelines. (3 marks)', 'Blood-stained gauze and cotton: infectious soiled waste - yellow bin. Used gloves and surgical mask: contaminated plastic waste - red bin. Syringe with needle and used scalpel blade: sharps - white (translucent) puncture-proof sharps container (needles not recapped). Empty plastic IV bottle: recyclable plastic waste - red bin. Broken glass ampoule: glassware - blue puncture-proof box. Leftover food and tissue paper: general, non-hazardous waste - black (or green for biodegradable) bin.', null, '[{"point": "Blood-stained gauze/cotton: infectious (soiled) waste - yellow bin", "marks": 0.5}, {"point": "Gloves and mask: contaminated recyclable plastic (or infectious) - red bin (per national guideline)", "marks": 0.5}, {"point": "Syringe with needle and scalpel blade: sharps - white/blue puncture-proof sharps container", "marks": 0.5}, {"point": "Empty IV bottle: non-infectious plastic / recyclable - red (or general recyclable)", "marks": 0.5}, {"point": "Broken glass ampoule: glassware - blue (puncture-proof) container", "marks": 0.5}, {"point": "Food and tissue: general (non-hazardous) waste - black/green bin", "marks": 0.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
